 "id": "harbor_phonebooth",
 "poem": "09",
 "name": "the booth on the harbour sidewalk",
 "look": "the same quay with a lit glass booth and a street lamp; suitcases at the curb; the abyss can open in the water behind",
 "light": "warm booth box and lamp pool against cold water; at dawn the booth goes dark and grey light takes over",
